 "notes": ["The input is the bytes of one validation report. The generator writes them to a file with the name context.name and gives the entry point the path of that file. args.file of null stands for a path with no file.","value.issues is each issue of the report: the two texts that a page shows.","A field loc or msg that is no text reads as (not text). A field that is absent reads as an empty text.","The reader takes the first 200 items of the list and then drops each item that is no object.","A field of a wrong type reads as an empty text, as 0, as false or as absent. A text has 500 characters or less. A character is one code point.","A refused vector is a file that the reader gets no list of issues from. refusal is the problem that a page shows.","A problem is an object. class is one of none, missing, unreadable, too large, not JSON, not an object, refused, unreachable and capped. capped is a notice: the reader stopped at a limit and kept what it read before.","text is the sentence that a page shows. A problem of the class not JSON has no text: its sentence ends with a message of the JSON reader of Python. It has start, the part of the sentence before that message."],
